{
  "name": "AKUH,N & KQ Partner to Boost African Medical Travel",
  "parent_id": 203313642253074,
  "group_id": "880b80df-db9f-4d6e-8768-4e85bb9e5163",
  "alternates": [],
  "created_at": "2026-07-31T09:55:26.360Z",
  "deleted_at": null,
  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-08-12T15:02:58.505Z",
  "published_at": "2026-08-12T15:02:58.491Z",
  "id": 203989509606634,
  "uuid": "4ae9af78-6d72-41e7-8ef1-c0b421790cc9",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "a72eb622-ade4-58ec-0d2e-7a81b8bd2846",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "31f3e569-4874-3125-2973-edb7dd594106",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The collaboration brings together Kenya Airways' regional flight network and AKUH's advanced medical expertise to create a coordinated system for patients seeking treatment in Kenya. The goal is to position the Kenya as a leading destination for quality healthcare within the continent.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Under the agreement, KQ Health will provide end-to-end logistical support for patients, including medical clearances before travel, in-flight medical assistance, and direct ambulance transfers from the airport to Aga Khan University Hospital, Nairobi. AKUH,N will receive and treat patients in key specialties such as oncology, cardiology, surgery, and critical care.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"This partnership makes it easier for patients from across Africa to access world-class healthcare without leaving the continent,\" said Rashid Khalani, the CEO of Aga Khan University Hospital, Nairobi.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"When patients get treatment closer home, it means more convenient travel for them and their families, familiar environment and culture to recover in and a sense of pride in the quality of care available at home.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Kenya Airways, CEO, Allan Kilavuka said, \"This is an example of how aviation can directly support healthcare access. By working with Aga Khan University Hospital, we're connecting people not just to destinations, but to essential services that can change lives.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Medical travel has become a growing need across Africa, with many patients still relying on overseas care. By coordinating transport and treatment locally, Kenya Airways and Aga Khan University Hospital aim to offer a safer, more affordable, and dignified alternative closer to home.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The partnership supports Kenya's Vision 2030 agenda to establish the country as a regional hub for health care excellence and innovation. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
